cific files.\"\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-437-        )\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-438-    return None\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-439-\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-440-\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py:441:def _check_git_push_force(tokens: List[str]) -> Optional[str]:\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-442-    \"\"\"Return a block reason if tokens are a `git push --force` / `-f`.\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-443-\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-444-    Does NOT block `--force-with-lease`, which is the safe alternative.\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-445-\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-446-    Post PLAN-019 P0-02: tokens are normalized (``sudo git …``,\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-447-    ``/usr/bin/git …``, ``\\\\git …`` all reach the same decision).\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-448-    \"\"\"\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-449-    tokens = _normalize_command_tokens(tokens)\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-450-    if len(tokens) < 3 or tokens[0] != \"git\" or tokens[1] != \"push\":\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-451-        return None\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-452-    for t in tokens[2:]:\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-453-        if t == \"--force\" or t == \"-f\":\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-454-            return (\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-455-                \"BLOCKED: `git push --force` is destructive. \"\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-456-                \"Use `git push --force-with-lease` to avoid overwriting \"\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-457-                \"unseen commits pushed by others.\"\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-458-            )\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-459-    return None\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-460-\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-461-\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-462-# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-463-# PLAN-152 error-handling-01 — shlex.ValueError bypass close (Codex R3)\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-464-# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-465-#\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-466-# Closes the destructive-command bypass where the NAIVE subcommand split\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-467-# (`_split_subcommands`, a quoting-blind regex) breaks inside quotes, so\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-468-# `rm -rf ~ \";\"` splits into an unbalanced-quote chunk shlex rejects — the\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-469-# token rules never see it, yet real bash runs `rm -rf ~` (the quoted `;`\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-470-# is a literal argument).\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-471-#\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-472-# Fix history:\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-473-#   R1 (regex rescan of the raw chunk)  — Codex R2 P2#1: false-positived\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-474-#     on quoted literals like `echo \"a && rm -rf /tmp\"`.\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-475-#   R2 (`shlex.split` the whole command, segment on control-op TOKENS) —\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-476-#     Codex R3: shlex.split neither separates ADJACENT operators\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-477-#     (`true&&rm` stays one token → `rm` hides → bypass) NOR preserves\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-478-#     quoting (a quoted standalone `;` in `echo ';' rm -rf /tmp` looks\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-479-#     like a real separator → false positive).\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-480-#   R3 (this) — a QUOTE-AWARE subcommand splitter: it walks the command\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-481-#     char-by-char, honoring single/double quotes + backslash escapes (so\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-482-#     a quoted metachar is NEVER a separator) and recognizing operators\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-483-#     with NO surrounding whitespace. Each subcommand it yields has\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-484-#     balanced quotes, so the per-subcommand `shlex.split` + token rules\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-485-#     are exact. Blocks `rm -rf ~ \";\"`, `true&&rm -rf ~ ';'`,\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-486-#     `git pull && rm -rf ~ \";\"`; ALLOWs `echo \"a && rm -rf /tmp\"`,\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-487-#     `echo ';' rm -rf /tmp`. Verified against a 16-case adversarial\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-488-#     battery.\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-489-#\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-490-# A genuinely-unbalanced command (no closing quote) yields a subcommand\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-491-# that still fails shlex → skipped → ALLOW; bash would syntax-error too,\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-492-# and the `_e3` whole-command gate (a DIFFERENT tokenizer) already blocks\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-493-# the parse-rejectable class upstream (debate C4's reason this is not a\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-494-# blanket fail-closed).\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-495-#\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-496-# Kill-switch: CEO_BASH_RAWSCAN=0 reverts to the pre-PLAN-152 skip\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-497-# behavior (default-ON; read from the import-time trusted_env snapshot,\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-498-# NOT live os.environ, so a late-set value cannot disarm it mid-op).\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-499-\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-500-_RAWSCAN_DISABLE_VAR = \"CEO_BASH_RAWSCAN\"\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-501-"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"34b005ba-8b89-4e2d-a38f-79b02c6d7b54","uuid":"ee420579-32ba-495a-b85f-acac4bfaf81b","timestamp":"2026-11-13T17:25:58.273Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":".claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py:358:def _check_rm_rf(tokens: List[str]) -> Optional[str]:\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-359-    \"\"\"Return a block reason if tokens match `rm` with -r AND -f.\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-360-\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-361-    Post PLAN-019 P0-01 + P0-02:\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-362-\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-363-    - Privilege prefixes (``sudo``/``doas``/``nocorrect``) + their flags\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-364-      are stripped via :func:`_normalize_command_tokens`.\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-365-    - Absolute-path invocations (``/bin/rm``) and escaped-alias\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-366-      invocations (``\\\\rm``) are normalized to ``rm`` by the same helper.\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-367-    - Long options ``--recursive``, ``-r`` (alias), ``--force`` and their\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-368-      ``=value`` forms are detected alongside the original short-form\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-369-      character scan (``-rf``, ``-fr``, ``-Rf``, etc.).\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-370-    \"\"\"\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-371-    tokens = _normalize_command_tokens(tokens)\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-372-    if not tokens or tokens[0] != \"rm\":\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-373-        return None\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-374-    has_r = False\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-375-    has_f = False\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-376-    for t in tokens[1:]:\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-377-        if not t.startswith(\"-\"):\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-378-            continue  # positional argument\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-379-        if t.startswith(\"--\"):\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-380-            # Long option: match exact names (+ optional =value tail).\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-381-            # The ``=value`` form on ``--recursive``/``--force`` is NON-\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-382-            # STANDARD for POSIX ``rm`` (which treats both as boolean\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-383-            # flags). Security-first interpretation: if someone types\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-3