it\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-467-# (`_split_subcommands`, a quoting-blind regex) breaks inside quotes, so\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-468-# `rm -rf ~ \";\"` splits into an unbalanced-quote chunk shlex rejects — the\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-469-# token rules never see it, yet real bash runs `rm -rf ~` (the quoted `;`\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-470-# is a literal argument).\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-471-#\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-472-# Fix history:\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-473-#   R1 (regex rescan of the raw chunk)  — Codex R2 P2#1: false-positived\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-474-#     on quoted literals like `echo \"a && rm -rf /tmp\"`.\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-475-#   R2 (`shlex.split` the whole command, segment on control-op TOKENS) —\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-476-#     Codex R3: shlex.split neither separates ADJACENT operators\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-477-#     (`true&&rm` stays one token → `rm` hides → bypass) NOR preserves\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-478-#     quoting (a quoted standalone `;` in `echo ';' rm -rf /tmp` looks\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-479-#     like a real separator → false positive).\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-480-#   R3 (this) — a QUOTE-AWARE subcommand splitter: it walks the command\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-481-#     char-by-char, honoring single/double quotes + backslash escapes (so\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-482-#     a quoted metachar is NEVER a separator) and recognizing operators\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-483-#     with NO surrounding whitespace. Each subcommand it yields has\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-484-#     balanced quotes, so the per-subcommand `shlex.split` + token rules\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-485-#     are exact. Blocks `rm -rf ~ \";\"`, `true&&rm -rf ~ ';'`,\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-486-#     `git pull && rm -rf ~ \";\"`; ALLOWs `echo \"a && rm -rf /tmp\"`,\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-487-#     `echo ';' rm -rf /tmp`. Verified against a 16-case adversarial\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-488-#     battery.\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-489-#\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-490-# A genuinely-unbalanced command (no closing quote) yields a subcommand\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-491-# that still fails shlex → skipped → ALLOW; bash would syntax-error too,\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-492-# and the `_e3` whole-command gate (a DIFFERENT tokenizer) already blocks\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-493-# the parse-rejectable class upstream (debate C4's reason this is not a\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-494-# blanket fail-closed).\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-495-#\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-496-# Kill-switch: CEO_BASH_RAWSCAN=0 reverts to the pre-PLAN-152 skip\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-497-# behavior (default-ON; read from the import-time trusted_env snapshot,\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-498-# NOT live os.environ, so a late-set value cannot disarm it mid-op).\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-499-\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-500-_RAWSCAN_DISABLE_VAR = \"CEO_BASH_RAWSCAN\"\n.claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/normalization.py-501-","numLines":144,"totalLines":144},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01F3yqhGpFj2B1jfBZxJTLKC","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
