{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ased4wsXYXU2Fov7qt4f3i","type":"tool_result","content":"430\t  - Signed condition 58 is the redactor offsets defect fixed above.\n431\t  - This release does not claim the cure of any other annex condition. The\n432\t    partial spool change above is not claimed as one.\n433\t  - **The rest stays open, and no release is assigned to their cure.**\n434\t  - The list is in the sources the `[1.4.2]` entry names.\n435\t- **The v1.4.2 rc.1 annex.** This release does not claim the cure of its\n436\t  three P1 findings or of its P2 findings, declared in the `[1.4.3]` entry.\n437\t- **The rest of the `[1.4.3]` Known-open stays open as written there**,\n438\t  except where this release changes it:\n439\t  - the restore and strict-mode defects (above; the restore defects\n440\t    partly);\n441\t  - the harness sub-check gaps and the sub-check delegation (above; the\n442\t    sub-check partly);\n443\t  - the plan-lifecycle names and the cost-envelope directory (above);\n444\t  - the Bash guard's indirect-execution case (above, partly);\n445\t  - the root `CLAUDE.md` exclusion (above, partly);\n446\t  - the audit spool (above, partly);\n447\t  - the Codex pin and Codex as a hook host (Security and governance,\n448\t    above, partly): a Codex CLI newer than the manifest version now passes\n449\t    on its declared version without a re-pin, and the pin range, which\n450\t    admitted up to 0.160.x, has no upper bound.\n451\t- **Audit files can be deleted by Claude Code.** Claude Code's cleanup\n452\t  sweep unlinks every top-level `*.jsonl` in each project directory that is\n453\t  older than the `cleanupPeriodDays` of the session running the sweep\n454\t  (default 30), the audit logs and their rotated archives included. There\n455\t  is no plan in this release with a structural cure. The maintainer settings\n456\t  template still ships 90; the framework repository's own settings now use\n457\t  3650, and installs do not receive that file. The protection is still a\n458\t  scheduled backup with `ceo-backup.sh`.\n459\t\n460\t### What an adopter should know before installing or upgrading\n461\t\n462\t- Coming from v1.4.2, read `[1.4.3]` too. Its notes apply.\n463\t- The requirements are unchanged: Claude Code 2.1.280 or later, Python 3.9\n464\t  or later, and Node.js 20 or later for the npm shim.\n465\t- A command that reaches `rm -rf`, `git reset --hard` or a forced\n466\t  `git push` indirectly may now be blocked, and so may a shell body the\n467\t  guard cannot parse. To turn the scan off, set\n468\t  `CEO_BASH_INDIRECT_GUARD=0`, or only the heuristics with\n469\t  `CEO_BASH_INDIRECT_HEURISTICS=0`, in the environment Claude Code starts\n470\t  with. Each disable is recorded once per session.\n471\t- If you patched a hook by hand, re-apply the patch to its module. The\n472\t  modules behind the seven kernel entry points, the five flat modules\n473\t  above and `_lib/adapters/live/` are kernel paths now: a sentinel alone\n474\t  no longer unlocks them; they need `CEO_KERNEL_OVERRIDE` with\n475\t  `CEO_KERNEL_OVERRIDE_ACK=I-ACCEPT`.\n476\t- If your code reads `Finding.start` and `Finding.end` from\n477\t  `secret_patterns.scan()`, they now index the text you passed in, not its\n478\t  NFKC form.\n479\t- Expect a yellow `main_checkout_state` in `/ceo-boot` when your main"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"34b005ba-8b89-4e2d-a38f-79b02c6d7b54","uuid":"410c4959-a815-4bb2-8659-1e67c475cb17","timestamp":"2026-11-13T17:28:49.726Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.nUJTgA/tree/CHANGELOG.md","content":"  - Signed condition 58 is the redactor offsets defect fixed above.\n  - This release does not claim the cure of any other annex condition. The\n    partial spool change above is not claimed as one.\n  - **The rest stays open, and no release is assigned to their cure.**\n  - The list is in the sources the `[1.4.2]` entry names.\n- **The v1.4.2 rc.1 annex.** This release does not claim the cure of its\n  three P1 findings or of its P2 findings, declared in the `[1.4.3]` entry.\n- **The rest of the `[1.4.3]` Known-open stays open as written there**,\n  except where this release changes it:\n  - the restore and strict-mode defects (above; the restore defects\n    partly);\n  - the harness sub-check gaps and the sub-check delegation (above; the\n    sub-check partly);\n  - the plan-lifecycle names and the cost-envelope directory (above);\n  - the Bash guard's indirect-execution case (above, partly);\n  - the root `CLAUDE.md` exclusion (above, partly);\n  - the audit spool (above, partly);\n  - the Codex pin and Codex as a hook host (Security and governance,\n    above, partly): a Codex CLI newer than the manifest version now passes\n    on its declared version without a re-pin, and the pin range, which\n    admitted up to 0.160.x, has no upper bound.\n- **Audit files can be deleted by Claude Code.** Claude Code's cleanup\n  sweep unlinks every top-level `*.jsonl` in each project directory that is\n  older than the `cleanupPeriodDays` of the session running the sweep\n  (default 30), the audit logs and their rotated archives included. There\n  is no plan in this release with a structural cure. The maintainer settings\n  template still ships 90; the framework repository's own settings now use\n  3650, and installs do not receive that file. The protection is still a\n  scheduled backup with `ceo-backup.sh`.\n\n### What an adopter should know before installing or upgrading\n\n- Coming from v1.4.2, read `[1.4.3]` too. Its notes apply.\n- The requirements are unchanged: Claude Code 2.1.280 or later, Python 3.9\n  or later, and Node.js 20 or later for the npm shim.\n- A command that reaches `rm -rf`, `git reset --hard` or a forced\n  `git push` indirectly may now be blocked, and so may a shell body the\n  guard cannot parse. To turn the scan off, set\n  `CEO_BASH_INDIRECT_GUARD=0`, or only the heuristics with\n  `CEO_BASH_INDIRECT_HEURISTICS=0`, in the environment Claude Code starts\n  with. Each disable is recorded once per session.\n- If you patched a hook by hand, re-apply the patch to its module. The\n  modules behind the seven kernel entry points, the five flat modules\n  above and `_lib/adapters/live/` are kernel paths now: a sentinel alone\n  no longer unlocks them; they need `CEO_KERNEL_OVERRIDE` with\n  `CEO_KERNEL_OVERRIDE_ACK=I-ACCEPT`.\n- If your code reads `Finding.start` and `Finding.end` from\n  `secret_patterns.scan()`, they now index the text you passed in, not its\n  NFKC form.\n- Expect a yellow `main_checkout_state` in `/ceo-boot` when your main","numLines":50,"startLine":430,"totalLines":2658}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Ased4wsXYXU2Fov7qt4f3i","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
